# The lifetimes module (spec §3.8, §3.16): what the std's natives hold and keep, which no code shows
# the analysis of lifetimes (§7). Both annotations stand only on the std's externs, since a host
# keeps no language values (§9).

# On an extern struct: a value of it holds what a value of `T` holds, a tuple listing several types
# and `()` none. Without it, a value holds its type arguments.
struct Holds<T>

# On an extern function: each parameter, by name, comes to hold the values of the parameters listed
# for it. Without it, a parameter taken by `&` keeps every other one, and nothing else is kept.
struct Keeps:
  into: Map<String, Array<String>>
